1
00:00:01,400 --> 00:00:04,375
By Friday, you can see through the barista.

2
00:00:04,395 --> 00:00:05,450
Not a little.

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:08,121
You can read the menu through his chest.

4
00:00:08,448 --> 00:00:10,154
He's been making your coffee for two

5
00:00:10,174 --> 00:00:10,978
years.

6
00:00:10,998 --> 00:00:12,756
You've never asked his name.

7
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:15,151
And he's not the only one.

8
00:00:18,201 --> 00:00:19,806
It starts on Monday.

9
00:00:19,826 --> 00:00:21,981
The man in the lift is a bit pale.

10
00:00:22,001 --> 00:00:23,611
You assume it's the lighting.

11
00:00:24,601 --> 00:00:27,056
On Tuesday, Dana is talking to you while

12
00:00:27,076 --> 00:00:28,906
you answer an email.

13
00:00:28,926 --> 00:00:31,181
Halfway through her sentence, you notice

14
00:00:31,201 --> 00:00:33,116
you can see the printer behind her.

15
00:00:33,136 --> 00:00:35,048
…so that's my news.

16
00:00:35,068 --> 00:00:36,294
What do you think?

17
00:00:36,314 --> 00:00:36,864
Great!

18
00:00:36,904 --> 00:00:37,209
Yeah.

19
00:00:37,229 --> 00:00:37,859
Great.

20
00:00:37,879 --> 00:00:39,518
I said my cat died.

21
00:00:40,268 --> 00:00:41,798
She fades a little more.

22
00:00:41,818 --> 00:00:43,147
You watch it happen.

23
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:43,597
Dana.

24
00:00:43,617 --> 00:00:44,332
Sorry.

25
00:00:44,352 --> 00:00:45,462
I wasn't listening.

26
00:00:45,482 --> 00:00:46,805
Tell me about your cat.

27
00:00:47,855 --> 00:00:49,110
She tells you.

28
00:00:49,130 --> 00:00:51,160
The cat was called Biscuit, and he hated

29
00:00:51,180 --> 00:00:52,955
everyone except her.

30
00:00:52,975 --> 00:00:54,805
With every sentence, she gets a little

31
00:00:54,825 --> 00:00:55,945
more solid.

32
00:00:55,965 --> 00:00:57,346
So that's the rule.

33
00:00:57,366 --> 00:00:59,470
Ignore someone, and they fade.

34
00:00:59,490 --> 00:01:01,530
Pay attention, and they come back.

35
00:01:02,520 --> 00:01:04,800
On Wednesday, your mum calls.

36
00:01:04,820 --> 00:01:06,575
You can see her kitchen tiles through

37
00:01:06,595 --> 00:01:07,477
her cheek.

38
00:01:07,497 --> 00:01:09,329
I won't keep you, I know you're busy.

39
00:01:09,349 --> 00:01:10,449
I'm not busy.

40
00:01:10,469 --> 00:01:11,578
Tell me everything.

41
00:01:11,598 --> 00:01:12,178
Everything?

42
00:01:12,198 --> 00:01:12,763
Well.

43
00:01:12,783 --> 00:01:14,188
The neighbour's cat got stuck in the

44
00:01:14,208 --> 00:01:15,092
bins again.

45
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:17,097
She talks for forty minutes.

46
00:01:17,117 --> 00:01:19,147
You hear about the cat, the bins and

47
00:01:19,167 --> 00:01:21,047
a cousin you have never met.

48
00:01:21,067 --> 00:01:23,955
By the end, she's as solid as her teapot.

49
00:01:25,605 --> 00:01:26,910
You get good at it.

50
00:01:26,930 --> 00:01:29,735
You learn the barista's name: Kofi.

51
00:01:29,755 --> 00:01:32,350
You ask the lift man about his dog.

52
00:01:32,370 --> 00:01:34,495
You stop typing when your boss talks,

53
00:01:34,515 --> 00:01:36,788
which surprises him more than anyone.

54
00:01:36,808 --> 00:01:37,658
Are you…

55
00:01:37,703 --> 00:01:38,479
listening?

56
00:01:38,499 --> 00:01:39,161
Yes.

57
00:01:39,181 --> 00:01:40,486
Nobody listens.

58
00:01:40,506 --> 00:01:42,314
This is very unsettling.

59
00:01:42,334 --> 00:01:44,129
What were you saying about the budget?

60
00:01:44,149 --> 00:01:44,479
I…

61
00:01:44,499 --> 00:01:45,604
don't remember.

62
00:01:45,624 --> 00:01:48,323
Nobody's ever asked a follow-up question.

63
00:01:48,473 --> 00:01:51,153
By Thursday, the city looks solid again.

64
00:01:51,173 --> 00:01:52,643
You're exhausted.

65
00:01:52,663 --> 00:01:54,773
Paying attention, it turns out, is a

66
00:01:54,793 --> 00:01:56,273
full-time job.

67
00:01:57,263 --> 00:01:59,713
On Friday night, you get home, drop

68
00:01:59,733 --> 00:02:01,992
onto the sofa, and open your phone.

69
00:02:02,012 --> 00:02:03,424
Did you see the score?

70
00:02:03,444 --> 00:02:04,280
Mm.

71
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:05,918
I said, did you see the

72
00:02:07,408 --> 00:02:08,445
You look up.

73
00:02:09,135 --> 00:02:10,715
You can see the cushions through your

74
00:02:10,735 --> 00:02:11,506
brother.

75
00:02:11,526 --> 00:02:12,481
Not a little.

76
00:02:12,501 --> 00:02:14,040
Almost all the way.

77
00:02:14,729 --> 00:02:16,159
You checked everyone.

78
00:02:16,179 --> 00:02:18,569
The barista, the lift, the boss.

79
00:02:18,589 --> 00:02:20,094
You never checked the person on your

80
00:02:20,114 --> 00:02:20,922
sofa.

81
00:02:21,972 --> 00:02:22,402
Theo.

82
00:02:22,422 --> 00:02:23,469
What score?

83
00:02:23,489 --> 00:02:24,517
Doesn't matter.

84
00:02:24,537 --> 00:02:25,182
It does.

85
00:02:25,202 --> 00:02:26,061
Who played?

86
00:02:26,081 --> 00:02:27,323
You hate football.

87
00:02:27,343 --> 00:02:28,043
I know.

88
00:02:28,063 --> 00:02:29,201
Tell me anyway.

89
00:02:30,251 --> 00:02:31,156
He tells you.

90
00:02:31,176 --> 00:02:32,156
All of it.

91
00:02:32,176 --> 00:02:34,366
The match, the referee, a goal he's

92
00:02:34,386 --> 00:02:35,966
still angry about.

93
00:02:35,986 --> 00:02:37,966
Then, somehow, his job interview on

94
00:02:37,986 --> 00:02:39,973
Monday, which you didn't know about.

95
00:02:39,993 --> 00:02:41,405
You've got an interview?

96
00:02:41,425 --> 00:02:42,080
I told you.

97
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:42,838
Twice.

98
00:02:42,858 --> 00:02:44,213
Tell me a third time.

99
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:45,446
I'm listening now.

100
00:02:45,466 --> 00:02:46,421
It's at a bike shop.

101
00:02:46,441 --> 00:02:47,401
I like bikes.

102
00:02:47,421 --> 00:02:48,765
You didn't know I like bikes.

103
00:02:48,785 --> 00:02:50,414
I didn't know you like bikes.

104
00:02:50,434 --> 00:02:52,436
I've liked bikes since I was six.

105
00:02:52,936 --> 00:02:54,216
Then we'll practise.

106
00:02:54,236 --> 00:02:56,528
What do they ask at bike shop interviews?

107
00:02:56,548 --> 00:02:58,208
Probably about bikes.

108
00:02:59,258 --> 00:03:01,238
By midnight, he's solid again.

109
00:03:01,258 --> 00:03:03,238
Fully, annoyingly solid.

110
00:03:03,258 --> 00:03:04,954
He's eaten all your crisps.

111
00:03:05,864 --> 00:03:06,169
Morning!

112
00:03:06,189 --> 00:03:07,070
The usual?

113
00:03:07,090 --> 00:03:08,250
Morning, Kofi.

114
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:09,492
How's your weekend?

115
00:03:09,642 --> 00:03:11,522
Kofi looks so surprised you think he

116
00:03:11,542 --> 00:03:12,875
might drop the cup.

117
00:03:12,895 --> 00:03:14,200
He doesn't fade.

118
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:15,825
Neither does anyone else.

119
00:03:15,845 --> 00:03:17,019
Not this week.

120
00:03:19,409 --> 00:03:21,089
Who would be fading around you right

121
00:03:21,109 --> 00:03:21,798
now?
